WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:05.750
It's always heartbreaking to discover that
the actors who’ve played your favorite characters

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:07.040
have passed away.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.460
Adding to our first list that you can find
on our YouTube channel, these actors have

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:12.910
also moved on without much public fanfare.

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:16.580
It doesn't matter whether these actors were
Hollywood royalty—they helped portray characters

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:18.020
we'll never forget.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.020
Richard Bonehill

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:23.220
While you might not recognize Richard Bonehill's
face, you'll recognize some of the characters

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:26.880
he's played over the years...especially if
you're a Star Wars fan.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.570
Bonehill's history as a competitive fencer
and swordsmanship coach landed him work on

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:33.050
Highlander, Flash Gordon, and Doctor Who.

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:36.490
He also played a variety of characters in
The Empire Strikes Back and Return of the

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:37.490
Jedi.

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:41.160
For the most part, he filled various background
roles, including multiple Stormtroopers and

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:42.640
Rebel Alliance soldiers.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:46.910
You'd probably best recognize him as Nien
Nunb, Lando Calrissian's alien co-pilot during

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:48.850
the attack on the second Death Star.

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:53.190
Bonehill passed away on February 4th, 2015
at the age of 67.

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.680
Earl Hindman

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:58.390
Earl Hindman had a relatively low-profile
show business career, appearing in movies

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:01.300
like Silverado, and The Taking of Pelham One
Two Three.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:05.630
Throughout the '70s and '80s, he starred as
Bob Reid in more than 450 episodes of Ryan's

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:06.630
Hope.

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:09.521
Most '90s kids will remember him as Wilson,
the mysterious-but-friendly neighbor of the

00:01:09.521 --> 00:01:11.760
Taylors on the hit sitcom Home Improvement.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:16.970
Hindman died on December 29, 2003 at the age
of 61 due to lung cancer.

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:18.310
Bernie Mac

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:21.830
One of the original Kings of Comedy, Bernie
Mac built his career with a stand-up routine

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:24.190
heavily influenced by Richard Pryor.

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:28.120
Many might recognize Mac as Ice Cube's neighbor,
Pastor Clever, in Friday.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:32.140
Mac went on to star in Charlie's Angels: Full
Throttle, Ocean's Eleven, and Transformers

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:35.080
before headlining his own sitcom, The Bernie
Mac Show.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:39.250
During the last years of his life, Mac suffered
from Sarcoidosis, which heavily affected his

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:40.250
lungs.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:44.420
He succumbed to pneumonia complications in
August 2008 at the age of 50.

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:46.159
Richard Attenborough

00:01:46.159 --> 00:01:50.350
Long before he founded an ill-fated amusement
park using the secrets of dino DNA, Richard

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:53.610
Attenborough was already an accomplished and
award-winning actor.

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:56.480
Attenborough starred alongside Steve McQueen
in The Great Escape.

00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:01.590
He also won two consecutive Golden Globe Awards
in 1967 and 1968 for his work in The Sand

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:03.460
Pebbles and Doctor Dolittle.

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:07.159
Younger filmgoers will never forget Attenborough
as John Hammond, whose ambitions led to the

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:08.770
creation of Jurassic Park.

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:13.100
But that's just one short chapter in a life
that ended in August of 2014 at the age of

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:17.540
90, after many great cinematic achievements,
on both sides of the camera.

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:19.099
Sage Stallone

00:02:19.099 --> 00:02:22.950
Rocky 5 is arguably the least loved film of
the iconic boxing series.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:26.550
But under its cheesier elements, there's still
a solid story about the champ going broke,

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:30.310
losing his ability to box, and nearly losing
his relationship with his son.

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:34.060
Sylvester Stallone brought his own 14-year-old
son, Sage, to play the part of Rocky Jr. in

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:35.200
the film.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:38.709
After college, Sage continued working in small,
low-key film projects.

00:02:38.709 --> 00:02:43.500
Unfortunately, Sage died in 2012 at the young
age of 36 due to a heart attack brought on

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:46.280
by coronary artery disease.

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:47.629
Chris Penn

00:02:47.629 --> 00:02:51.099
The younger brother of veteran actor Sean
Penn, Chris Penn followed in his sibling's

00:02:51.099 --> 00:02:54.489
footsteps, breaking into Hollywood at the
tender age of 12.

00:02:54.489 --> 00:02:58.830
Penn is best remembered for his portrayal
of mob scion Nice Guy Eddie in Reservoir Dogs.

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:02.840
He also appeared in Footloose, Rush Hour,
Kiss Kiss Bang Bang, and Grand Theft Auto:

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:03.880
San Andreas.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:09.520
He died on January 24, 2006 at the age of
40 due to cardiomyopathy, with morphine, valium,

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:12.840
marijuana, and codeine all found in his body.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:17.129
Sean Penn attributes Chris' death to the weight
he visibly gained during the '90s.

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:18.519
Richard Griffiths

00:03:18.519 --> 00:03:23.150
A veteran stage, film, and television actor,
Richard Griffiths is known most for his portrayal

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:25.730
of Harry Potter's awful uncle, Vernon Dursley.

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:29.430
Outside of the Harry Potter series, Griffiths
won a slew of awards for his portrayal of

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:32.980
English teacher Douglas Hector in a play called
The History Boys.

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:37.250
He also starred in a variety of projects,
including Superman 2, Gandhi, Sleepy Hollow,

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:39.870
King Ralph, and The Hitchhiker's Guide to
the Galaxy.

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:45.209
Griffiths passed away at 65 on March 28, 2013
due to complications shortly after having

00:03:45.209 --> 00:03:46.740
heart surgery.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:48.510
James Avery

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:52.269
Whether you call him the Big Guy or Uncle
Phil, James Avery became a household name

00:03:52.269 --> 00:03:55.190
through his portrayal of Philip Banks on The
Fresh Prince of Bel-Air.

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:58.760
The burly actor had plenty of small roles
throughout his TV career, but was also known

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:00.360
for his voice acting work.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:04.700
He was the voice of War Machine on Iron Man
and Shredder on Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles:

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:06.760
"Well what is it?"

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:11.300
Avery also did voices for The Prince of Egypt,
The Real Ghostbusters, Fist of the North Star,

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.280
and Hulk Hogan's Rock 'n' Wrestling.

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:17.750
Like Richard Griffiths, Avery died from complications
following heart surgery in 2013 at the age

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:19.239
of 68.

00:04:19.239 --> 00:04:23.849
Thank you for always being a stern, funny,
and loving father figure on TV, Uncle Phil.

00:04:23.849 --> 00:04:25.300
Lou Albano and Danny Wells

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:31.689
"Captain" Lou Albano and Danny Wells entertained
millions of children from 1989-1991 on The

00:04:31.689 --> 00:04:33.509
Super Mario Bros. Super Show.

00:04:33.509 --> 00:04:37.919
The program featured Nintendo cartoons, bookended
by Albano and Wells playing the two beloved

00:04:37.919 --> 00:04:40.699
plumber brothers during live-action sequences
at their Brooklyn residence.

00:04:40.699 --> 00:04:44.009
Albano and Wells also voiced the animated
versions of Mario and Luigi during the Super

00:04:44.009 --> 00:04:45.009
Show cartoons.

00:04:45.009 --> 00:04:48.499
Captain Lou was a WWE Hall of Fame member
with a prominent professional wrestling career

00:04:48.499 --> 00:04:51.509
that started in 1953 and ended in 1995.

00:04:51.509 --> 00:04:57.020
Albano died on October 14, 2009 from a heart
attack at the age of 76.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:05:02.039
He left behind a wrestling legacy that includes
one of his grand-nephews, former MMA/UFC fighter

00:05:02.039 --> 00:05:04.229
and professional wrestler Phil Baroni.

00:05:04.229 --> 00:05:08.349
Danny Wells, who played Luigi, was known for
his TV guest appearances on the likes of The

00:05:08.349 --> 00:05:11.819
Jeffersons, Happy Days, Punky Brewster, Chips,
and The A-Team.

00:05:11.819 --> 00:05:15.729
He also did voice acting for Heathcliff, Batman:
The Animated Series, and more.

00:05:15.729 --> 00:05:18.629
He died of undisclosed causes on November
28, 2013.

00:05:18.629 --> 00:05:21.129
Richard Harris

00:05:21.129 --> 00:05:24.869
Yet another major loss to the cast of the
Harry Potter series, Richard Harris played

00:05:24.869 --> 00:05:28.259
Albus Dumbledore in The Sorcerer's Stone and
The Chamber of Secrets.

00:05:28.259 --> 00:05:32.559
Outside of Hogwarts, Harris was also an accomplished
singer, actor, director, writer, producer,

00:05:32.559 --> 00:05:33.559
and songwriter.

00:05:33.559 --> 00:05:37.439
Harris won Grammy and Golden Globe awards
for his work on 15 different albums and more

00:05:37.439 --> 00:05:42.659
than 70 films, including Camelot, The Guns
of Navarone, Gulliver's Travels, Patriot Games,

00:05:42.659 --> 00:05:46.159
Unforgiven, Gladiator, and The Count of Monte
Cristo.

00:05:46.159 --> 00:05:50.690
After being diagnosed with Hodgkin's disease,
Harris died on October 25, 2002 at the age

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:52.150
of 72.

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:53.150
Thanks for watching!

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:56.099
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:05:56.099 --> 00:05:58.509
And leave us a comment to let us know which
actors you want the world to remember...

